    {
      "item": "lem-lichtenbaum-schlessinger-complex-and-cotangent-ext",
      "finding": "F2 says the Lichtenbaum–Schlessinger complex 'admits a canonical map L_{B/A} to L_• in D(B) inducing an isomorphism τ≥−2 L_{B/A} to L_•', but attaches citations to def-cotangent-complex-of-a-ring-map, lem-cotangent-complex-resolution-independence and def-standard-resolution-of-a-ring-map. Those opened suppliers construct and compare polynomial-resolution cotangent complexes; they do not state the Lichtenbaum–Schlessinger comparison. Proof 1.2 separately cites the matching [Stacks Lemma 92.13.3, tag 09CG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09CG), whose statement and complete printed proof were opened. The concern is the attribution in F2, not a counterexample to the comparison.",
      "severity": "presentation"
    }
  ],
