    {
      "from": "reductive-affine-invariant-theory-and-geometric-quotients",
      "to": "algebraic-group-actions-orbits-stabilizers-and-controlled-quotients",
      "faithful": true,
      "note": "The stabilizer and translated-fibre uses preserve finite type, separated target and rational-point hypotheses. The connected orbit supplier is applied only after smoothness and connectedness are supplied; locally closed irreducible orbits are explicitly established in its Proof 1.1. The owned lemma separately proves the disconnected-group extension."
    },
    {
      "from": "algebraic-spaces-stacks-and-derived-algebraic-geometry-foundations",
